>
  <p>Nuvellum is an independent international publication concerned with the forces that shape public life and private attention: world affairs, business, technology, culture, film, sport and ideas. Its purpose is not merely to report what happened, but to examine what it means, what preceded it, and what may remain after the headline has passed.</p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>Reporting, analysis, explainers, opinion, reviews and cultural coverage are treated as distinct forms, each with its own obligations. The nature of a piece should never be left for the reader to discover by accident.</p>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Reporting should remain traceable to its sources, serious claims should withstand a higher degree of scrutiny, and material errors should be corrected plainly when they alter what a reader ought to understand.</p>
  <h2>How Nuvellum operates</h2>
  <p>Nuvellum is an independently operated publication using both editorial writing and automation-assisted news production. Nuvellum Global Desk is an institutional byline, not a claim that a particular reporter witnessed events. Material claims drawn from another newsroom or institution should identify that source in the article text.</p>
  <p>Automated checks cannot establish independent facts or substitute for an editor on sensitive stories. Readers can report factual concerns through the Corrections page.</p>
  <span slot="aside">Beyond the headline is not a promise of length, but of depth. Nuvellum exists for the part of the story that remains after the alert has vanished.</span>
</InstitutionalPage>
